          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The original articles explaining what is now called the Higgs mechanism by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneous symmetry breaking
            were
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                P. Anderson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Plasmons, gauge invariance and mass
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fran%C3%A7ois+Englert"}> François Englert
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Brout"} Robert Brout
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Broken Symmetry and the Mass of Gauge Vector Mesons
            %li
              %p
                Gerald Guralnik, C. R. Hagen, ; T. W. B. Kibble,
                %em Global Conservation Laws and Massless Particles
                Physical Review (1964)
            %li#Higgs64
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Higgs"}> Peter Higgs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Broken Symmetries and the Masses of Gauge Bosons
          %p
            While all these articles essentially describe the Higgs mechanism, apparently only the one by Peter Higgs explicitly points out that this mechanism predicts the existence of a new, then unobserved, boson, the one therefore now called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Higgs boson
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#PDG18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Particle+Data+Group"}> Particle Data Group
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://pdg.lbl.gov/"} Review of particle physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Status of Higgs Boson Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://pdg.lbl.gov/2018/reviews/rpp2018-rev-higgs-boson.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/StatusOfHiggsBosonPhysics2018.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antonio+Pich"}> Antonio Pich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Electroweak Symmetry Breaking and the Higgs Boson
                %a{:href => "https://www.actaphys.uj.edu.pl/index_n.php?I=R&V=47&N=1#151"} Acta Phys. Pol. B 47, 151
                (2016) (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.08749"}> arXiv:1512.08749
                )
            %li
              %p
                Sally Dawson, Christoph Englert, Tilman Plehn,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higgs Physics: It ain’t over till it’s over
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.01324"} arXiv:1808.01324
            %li
              %p
                Jochem Kip, Ronald Kleiss,
                %em The Higgs Mechanism with Diagrams: a didactic approach
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.08329"}> arXiv:2404.08329
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (discussion via
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
          %p
            Review of the general theory of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneous symmetry breaking
          %ul
            %li
              Jeremy Bernstein,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Spontaneous symmetry breaking, gauge theories, the Higgs mechanism and all that
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.calstatela.edu/faculty/kaniol/p544/rmp46_p7_higgs_goldstone.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
            of Higgs
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+particle+physics%29"} models
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Marcela Carena, Howard E. Haber,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higgs Boson Theory and Phenomenology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0208209"} arXiv:hep-ph/0208209
          %p
            Discussion in “string localized”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
            and claim of derivation of the quartic form of the Higgs potential:
          %ul
            %li
              Jens Mund, Karl-Henning Rehren,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Schroer"} Bert Schroer
              %em How the Higgs potential got its shape
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.06133"}> arXiv:2209.06133
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#detection Detection
          %p
            Early discussion of the detection of a Higgs field of 125
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GeV"} GeV
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Gibbs11a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Gibbs"}> Philip Gibbs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Seminar Watch (Higgs Special), Rumoured Higgs at 125 GeV and What Would a Higgs at 125 GeV Tell Us?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://prespacetime.com/index.php/pst/article/view/308/298"} web
            %li#HLL11
              %p
                Martin Holthausen, Kher Sham Lim, Manfred Lindner,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Planck Scale Boundary Conditions and the Higgs Mass
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.2415"} arXiv:1112.2415
          %p
            The official announcement of the detection at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#ATLAS12
              %p
                G. Aad et al. (ATLAS Collaboration),
                %em Observation of a New Particle in the Search for the Standard Model Higgs Boson with the ATLAS Detector at the LHC,
                Phys. Lett. B 716, 1 (2012) (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.7214"}> arXiv:1207.7214
                )
            %li#CMS12
              %p
                S. Chatrchyan et al. (CMS Collaboration),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Observation of a New Boson at a Mass of 125 GeV with the CMS Experiment at the LHC
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.7235"} arXiv:1207.7235
            %li#ATLAS15
              %p
                G. Aad et al. (ATLAS Collaboration, CMS Collaboration),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Combined Measurement of the Higgs Boson Mass in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p p
                    Collisions at
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msqrt
                            %mi s
                          %mo =
                          %mn 7
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{s} = 7
                    and 8 TeV with the ATLAS and CMS Experiments
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1503.07589"} arXiv:1503.07589
          %h3#ReferencesVacuumInstability Vacuum (in-)stability
          %p
            Before experimental observation of the Higgs mass at the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+stability"} vacuum stability
            were analyzed in
          %ul
            %li#EEGHR09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Ellis"}> John Ellis
                , J.R. Espinosa,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gian+Giudice"} Gian Giudice
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Probable Fate of the Standard Model
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.0954"} arXiv:0906.0954
            %li#Gibbs11b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Gibbs"}> Philip Gibbs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://vixra.wordpress.com/2011/12/04/what-would-a-higgs-at-125-gev-tell-us/"} What would a Higgs at 125 GeV tell us?
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Seminar Watch (Higgs Special), Rumoured Higgs at 125 GeV and What Would a Higgs at 125 GeV Tell Us?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://prespacetime.com/index.php/pst/article/view/308/298"} web
          %p
            More discussion of the near-criticality of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+stability"} vacuum stability
            after the observation of the Higgs mass is due to
          %ul
            %li#DVEEGI12
              Giuseppe Degrassi, Stefano Di Vita, Joan Elias-Miró, José R. Espinosa,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gian+Giudice"} Gian Giudice
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higgs mass and vacuum stability in the Standard Model at NNLO
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1205.6497"} arrXiv:1205.6497
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP08%282012%29098"} doi:10.1007/JHEP&amp;lpar;2012&amp;rpar;098
          %p with a more precise analysis due to
          %ul
            %li#BKPV15
              A. V. Bednyakov, B. A. Kniehl, A. F. Pikelner, and O. L. Veretin,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stability of the Electroweak Vacuum: Gauge Independence and Advanced Precision
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.08833"} arXiv:1507.08833
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.115.201802"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.115.201802
          %p
            Careful discussion of the stability issue under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Anders Andreassen, William Frost, Matthew D. Schwartz,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Consistent Use of the Standard Model Effective Potential
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.0292"} arXiv:1408.0292
          %p
            and with emphasis on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
            in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+tunneling"} quantum tunneling
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+decay"} vacuum decay
          %ul
            %li#AFFS17
              Anders Andreassen, David Farhi, William Frost, Matthew D. Schwartz,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Precision decay rate calculations in quantum field theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.06090"} arXiv:1604.06090
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li#Kusenko15
              %p
                Alexander Kusenko,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://physics.aps.org/articles/v8/108"} Are We on the Brink of the Higgs Abyss?
            %li
              %p
                Sebastian Baum,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the metastability of the Standard Model
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://uu.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:819933/FULLTEXT01.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Holger Gies,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Vacuum stability and the mass of the Higgs boson
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://physik.uni-graz.at/~dk-user/talks/Gies_20150828.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Schwartz15
              %p
                Matthew Schwartz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Do we know if our universe is stable?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.physics.rutgers.edu/het/video/schwartz15a.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Strumia17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Strumia"}> Alessandro Strumia
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higgs and Vacuum (In)Stability
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/660870/contributions/2746200/attachments/1538374/2411246/2017-HiggsDecay.pdf"} pdf
            %li#AFS18
              %p
                Anders Andreassen, William Frost, Matthew D. Schwartz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Scale Invariant Instantons and the Complete Lifetime of the Standard Model
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.08124"} arXiv:1707.08124
          %p Speculation about what this near-criticality of the Higgs vacuum could be pointing to:
          %p
            attractor mechanism in a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of vacua
          %ul
            %li#BDGGSSS13
              Dario Buttazzo, Giuseppe Degrassi, Pier Paolo Giardino,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gian+Giudice"} Gian Giudice
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Strumia"} Alessandro Strumia
              = succeed "," do
                %em Investigating the near-criticality of the Higgs boson
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1307.3536"} arXiv:1307.3536
          %p
            an
            = succeed "-extension" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-MSSM"} G₂-MSSM
          %ul
            %li#IsidoriPattori17
              Gino Isidori, Andrea Pattori,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  On the tuning in the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mi h
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m_h, m_t)
                  plane: Standard Model criticality vs. High-scale SUSY
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.11060"} arXiv:1710.11060
          %p
            as well as
            %a{:href => "#Kane18"} Kane 18, “Clue 4”
          %p
            and more generally in view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+supersymmetry"} split supersymmetry
          %ul
            %li#GiudiceStrumia11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gian+Giudice"}> Gian Giudice
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Strumia"} Alessandro Strumia
              = succeed "," do
                %em Probing High-Scale and Split Supersymmetry with Higgs Mass Measurements
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1108.6077"} arXiv:1108.6077
          %p
            Arguments that a false Higgs vacuum is incompatible with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmological
            evolution (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inflation"}> inflation
            ) include the following:
          %ul
            %li#EGR07
              %p
                J.R. Espinosa,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gian+Giudice"} Gian Giudice
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmological implications of the Higgs mass measurement
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0710.2484"} arXiv:0710.2484
            %li#HKSZ14
              %p
                Anson Hook, John Kearney, Bibhushan Shakya, Kathryn M. Zurek,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Probable or Improbable Universe? Correlating Electroweak Vacuum Instability with the Scale of Inflation
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.5953"} arXiv:1404.5953
            %li#EGMRSST15
              %p
                Jose R. Espinosa,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gian+Giudice"} Gian Giudice
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Strumia"} Alessandro Strumia
                %em The cosmological Higgstory of the vacuum instability
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.04825"}> arXiv:1505.04825
                )
            %li#EKSYZ16
              %p
                William E. East, John Kearney, Bibhushan Shakya, Hojin Yoo, Kathryn M. Zurek,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spacetime Dynamics of a Higgs Vacuum Instability During Inflation
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1607.00381"} arXiv:1607.00381
          %p But see
          %ul
            %li
              Mark P. Hertzberg, Mudit Jain,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Explanation for why the Early Universe was Stable and Dominated by the Standard Model
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.04648"} arXiv:1911.04648
          %p
            for a possible solution by strong
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            between the Higgs field and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inflaton"} inflaton
          %p
            An interpretation in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+safety"} asymptotic safety
          %ul
            %li#ShaposhnikovWetterich09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shaposhnikov"}> Mikhail Shaposhnikov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christof+Wetterich"} Christof Wetterich
              = succeed "," do
                %em Asymptotic safety of gravity and the Higgs boson mass
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0208"} arXiv:0912.0208
          %p
            Proposals for further
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiments"} experiments
          %ul
            %li
              Roberto Franceschini,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Strumia"} Alessandro Strumia
              = succeed "," do
                %em The collider landscape: which collider for establishing the SM instability?
              %strong 2022
              229 (2022) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.17197"}> arXiv:2203.17197
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP08(2022)229"} doi:10.1007/JHEP08(2022)229
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Thomas Steingasser, David I. Kaiser,
                %em Higgs Criticality beyond the Standard Model
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.10361"}> arXiv:2307.10361
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gudrun+Hiller"}> Gudrun Hiller
                , Tim Höhne, Daniel F. Litim, Tom Steudtner,
                %em Vacuum Stability in the Standard Model and Beyond
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.08811"}> arXiv:2401.08811
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Thomas Steingasser,
                %em Higgs criticality in and beyond the Standard Model
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.02415"}> arXiv:2405.02415
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Strumia"}> Alessandro Strumia
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Higgs boson and the possible instability in its potential
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/AgXGKPiB9y0"} video
          %h3#diphoton_decay Diphoton decay
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            of the
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+field"} Higgs field
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pawel+Duch"}> Pawel Duch
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duetsch"} Michael Duetsch
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jose+Gracia-Bondia"} Jose Gracia-Bondia
              %em Diphoton decay of the higgs from the Epstein–Glaser viewpoint
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.12675"}> arXiv:2011.12675
              )
          %h3#gaugehiggs_unification_2 Gauge-Higgs unification
          %p
            Discussion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge-Higgs+unification"} gauge-Higgs unification
          %p The mechanism is due to
          %ul
            %li#Manton79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Manton"}> Nicholas Manton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A new six-dimensional approach to the Weinberg-Salam model
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(79)90192-5"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(79)90192-5
            %li#Hosotani83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yutaka+Hosotani"}> Yutaka Hosotani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dynamical Mass Generation by Compact Extra Dimensions
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/188768"} spire:188768
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(83)90170-3"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(83)90170-3
            %li#Hosotani89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yutaka+Hosotani"}> Yutaka Hosotani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dynamics of non-integrable phases and gauge symmetry breaking
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0003-4916(89)90015-8"} doi:10.1016/0003-4916(89)90015-8
          %p and was revived with:
          %ul
            %li
              H. Hatanaka, T. Inami, C.S. Lim,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Gauge Hierarchy Problem and Higher Dimensional Gauge Theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9805067"} arXiv:hep-th/9805067
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Hosotani12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yutaka+Hosotani"}> Yutaka Hosotani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gauge-Higgs Unification Approach
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.0552"} arXiv:1206.0552
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Naoyuki Haba, Kazunori Takenaga, Toshifumi Yamashita,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higgs mass in the gauge-Higgs unification
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0411250"} arXiv:hep-ph/0411250
            %li#Lim09
              %p
                C. S. Lim,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Precision Tests and CP Violation in Gauge-Higgs Unification
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.iop.vast.ac.vn/theor/conferences/icfp09/files/Lim"} slides pdf
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge-Higgs+unification"} gauge-Higgs unification
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%2811%29"} Spin(11)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
            (“SO(11)-GUT”):
          %ul
            %li#HosotaniYamatsu15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yutaka+Hosotani"}> Yutaka Hosotani
                , Naoki Yamatsu,
                = succeed "," do
